      {
        "id": "def-marchenko-pastur-measure",
        "kind": "definition",
        "title": "Marchenko–Pastur measure with aspect ratio gamma",
        "deps": [
          "def-countable-choice",
          "def-borel-sigma-algebra",
          "def-dirac-measure",
          "def-lebesgue-measure-and-the-lebesgue-sigma-algebra"
        ],
        "dependency_level": 0,
        "justified_by": [
          "lem-marchenko-pastur-formula-defines-a-finite-measure"
        ],
      "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice.\n\nFor $\\gamma>0$, set\n$$a_\\gamma=(1-\\sqrt\\gamma)^2,\\qquad b_\\gamma=(1+\\sqrt\\gamma)^2,\\qquad r_+:=\\max\\{r,0\\}\\quad(r\\in\\mathbb R).$$\nDefine the Marchenko–Pastur set function on Borel $A\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ by\n$$\\mu_\\gamma(A):=\\int_{A\\cap(a_\\gamma,b_\\gamma)}\\frac{\\sqrt{(b_\\gamma-x)(x-a_\\gamma)}}{2\\pi\\gamma x}\\,d\\lambda(x)+\\left(1-\\frac1\\gamma\\right)_+\\delta_0(A),$$\nwhere $\\lambda$ is Lebesgue measure on $\\mathbb R$. The formula defines a finite Borel measure; its total mass is established by the Marchenko–Pastur law below."
      },
      {
