      },
      {
        "id": "lem-adapted-resolvent-trace-concentration",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "title": "Adapted resolvent-trace martingale concentration for independent columns",
        "deps": [
          "lem-rank-one-resolvent-update-and-trace-bound",
          "thm-mcdiarmid-bounded-differences",
          "cor-first-borel-cantelli-lemma-for-events",
          "def-axiom-of-choice"
        ],
        "dependency_level": 1,
      "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice, and let all random vectors below be defined on one common probability space. For each positive integer $n$, let $d_n$ be a positive integer, let $Y_{n,1},\\ldots,Y_{n,n}$ be independent random vectors in $\\mathbb R^{d_n}$, let $B_n=\\sum_{j=1}^{n}Y_{n,j}Y_{n,j}^{\\mathsf T}$, and let $z=u+i\\eta$ with fixed $u\\in\\mathbb R$ and $\\eta>0$. Define\n$$M_n(z):=\\frac1{d_n}\\operatorname{tr}(B_n-zI)^{-1}.$$\nIf $d_n/n\\to c$ for some $c\\in(0,\\infty)$, then $M_n(z)-\\mathbb E[M_n(z)]\\to0$ almost surely. More precisely, for every $t>0$,\n$$\\Pr\\left\\{|M_n(z)-\\mathbb E M_n(z)|>t\\right\\} \\le4\\exp\\left(-\\frac{t^2d_n^2\\eta^2}{4n}\\right).$$"
      },
      {
        "id": "lem-marchenko-pastur-formula-defines-a-finite-measure",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "title": "The Marchenko–Pastur formula defines a probability law with the fixed-point transform",
        "deps": [
          "def-countable-choice",
          "def-marchenko-pastur-measure",
          "thm-lebesgue-measure-is-a-complete-measure",
          "thm-borel-sets-are-lebesgue-measurable",
          "thm-indefinite-integral-of-a-nonnegative-function-is-a-measure",
          "thm-identity-theorem-holomorphic-functions",
          "thm-dominated-convergence"
        ],
        "dependency_level": 1
      },
      {
        "id": "lem-stieltjes-transform-inversion-and-uniqueness-on-the-real-line",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "title": "Stieltjes inversion and uniqueness for probability measures on the real line",
        "deps": [
          "def-countable-choice",
          "def-stieltjes-transform-of-a-real-probability-measure",
          "def-lebesgue-measure-and-the-lebesgue-sigma-algebra",
          "thm-lebesgue-measure-is-a-complete-measure",
          "thm-borel-sets-are-lebesgue-measurable",
          "thm-tonelli-theorem-for-sigma-finite-product-spaces",
          "thm-fubini-theorem-for-l-one-on-sigma-finite-product-spaces",
          "thm-dominated-convergence",
          "thm-dynkin-pi-lambda"
        ],
        "dependency_level": 1,
      "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice.\n\nLet $\\mu$ be a Borel probability measure on $\\mathbb R$, with Stieltjes transform $m_\\mu(z)=\\int (x-z)^{-1}\\,d\\mu(x)$ for $\\operatorname{Im}z>0$. For every $a<b$ and $x\\in\\mathbb R$,\n$$\\mu((a,b))+\\tfrac12\\mu(\\{a\\})+\\tfrac12\\mu(\\{b\\})=\\lim_{\\eta\\downarrow0}\\frac1\\pi\\int_a^b\\operatorname{Im}m_\\mu(u+i\\eta)\\,du,\\qquad \\mu(\\{x\\})=\\lim_{\\eta\\downarrow0}\\eta\\,\\operatorname{Im}m_\\mu(x+i\\eta).$$\nIf two Borel probability measures on $\\mathbb R$ have the same Stieltjes transform on the upper half-plane, then they are equal."
      },
      {
        "id": "lem-nested-iid-fourth-moment-truncation-and-diagonal-control",
        "kind": "lemma",
